# LeakSanitizer suppressions for make test-asan.
#
# Only proven third-party false positives belong here, each with the
# evidence. A leak in this repository's code is fixed, never listed.

# libvirt registers its object classes (virConnect, virDomain and the rest)
# once per process, in a virOnce/pthread_once initialiser that
# virConnectOpen runs on first use, and never frees them: they live as
# long as the process. Every libvirt suite reports the same 8 allocations,
# 263 bytes, whether it opens one connection or many, all under
# virClassNew <- virOnce <- virGetConnect <- virConnectOpen. A leak per
# connection would grow with the connections.
leak:virClassNew
